w: Shake off dull sloth, and joy- ful rise, To pay thy morn- ing sac- ri- fice. 
w: Im- prove thy tal- ent with due care; For the great day thy- self pre- pare. 
w: Re- flect all Heaven's pro- pit- ious ways In ar- dent love, and cheer- ful praise. 
w: Think how all see- ing God thy ways And all thy sec- ret thoughts sur- veys. 
w: Who all night long un- wear- ied sing High praise to the e- ter- nal King. 
w: Grant, Lord, when I from death shall wake I may of end- less light par- take.
w: For to my soul 'tis hell to be But for one mo- ment void of Thee.
w: Guard my first springs of thought and will, And with Thy- self my spi- rit fill.
w: That all my powers, with all their might, In Thy sole glo- ry may u- nite.
w: Wert Thou not there to be en- joyed, And I in hymns to be em- ployed.
w: Praise Him a- bove, ye heaven- ly host; Praise Fa- ther, Son, and Ho- ly Ghost.
